      "title": "Recommendation",
      "content": "Provision each agent host to support a minimum of 1,200 concurrent tool operations, with the following specific configurations: (1) Implement 78-way sharding for the pipeline pool, 10-way for attention, 18-way for quantization, and 75-way for softmax to eliminate the most critical contention points; (2) Increase dataset memory budget to 62 and attention latency budget to 39 as per team recommendations; (3) Choose hardware with at least 64 logical cores and multiple NUMA domains to accommodate the high sharding factor without cross‑node traffic; (4) Monitor real‑time utilization metrics to ensure backlog stays below 1,150 per second and shard utilization remains under 30 percent, adjusting capacity upward as workload grows. This approach aligns cost directly with tool work, maximizes throughput, and prevents regressions that would increase per‑workflow cost.",
