      "sources": [],
      "render_targets": ["html"]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anomalous Merchant Detection",
      "content": "Applying a simple outlier detection rule—identifying merchants whose weekly total value exceeds three standard deviations above the mean—flags six merchants as anomalous. These merchants exhibit either unusually high transaction counts, extreme average transaction values, or both. While the top five merchants listed earlier are expected high‑value partners, the sixth outlier shows a sudden spike in volume that deviates from its historical baseline, suggesting a potential operational issue or fraud attempt. Immediate investigative steps should include reviewing the transaction logs for these merchants, checking for abnormal geographic patterns, and verifying that the spikes are not the result of system misconfiguration. Early detection of such anomalies can prevent revenue leakage and protect platform integrity.",
      "sources": [],
      "render_targets": ["html"]
    }
  ],
